  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\nMid level trof to drop down across the region and through the upper \nOhio Valley Friday with a low closing off over the Great Lakes Friday\nnight into Saturday. This system will bring a chance of showers \nFriday. Precipitation will be light and scattered with the best\nchance across the north during the morning.  \n\nA secondary frontal passage will also usher in a somewhat cooler \nairmass heading into the weekend. Daytime highs will only be in the \n50s Saturday and Sunday. Frost will be possible Friday night with \nlows in the mid 30s. Frost and freezing conditions will also be \npossible Saturday night and Sunday night with lows expected to be\nin the lower and middle 30s.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2)\n\nA dry forecast is expected after Friday through most of next week \nas northwest flow aloft becomes more westerly. Starting Monday, \ntemperatures will modify a little each day, generally in the low to \nmid 60s for highs and mid-upper 30s for lows. The next chance for\nrain looks to hold off until next Thursday - followed by cooler \ntemperatures next weekend.",
